nd errors (queue 242; Python/initconfig.c's config_get_stdio_errors and"] [203 1 "// pylifecycle.c's create_stdio): PYTHONIOENCODING=ENCODING[:ERRORS] (ignored under -E and -I) forces the encoding and"] [204 1 "// the errors of stdin and stdout; stderr's errors stay backslashreplace. Without ERRORS they are strict, and"] [205 1 "// surrogateescape when no encoding is forced and config_get_stdio_errors says so (stdioErrorsEscape, queue 595: UTF-8"] [206 1 "// mode, the C or POSIX locale, a coercion target such as musl's default C.UTF-8)."] [210 2 "// forced: the encoding PYTHONIOENCODING gave, named by its codec once the codecs run (stdioCodecName)"] [243 1 "// stdioErrorsEscape is config_get_stdio_errors' surrogateescape (queue 595): in UTF-8 mode, and when LC_CTYPE's locale"] [244 1 "// (setlocale(LC_CTYPE, \"\") as musl names it: C.UTF-8 when no variable sets one) is the C or POSIX locale or a locale"] [245 1 "// coercion target (C.UTF-8, C.utf8, UTF-8: PY_COERCE_C_LOCALE, configure's on Linux); else strict."] [257 1 "// stdioCodecName is init_stdio_encoding's config_get_codec_name (queue 595): PYTHONIOENCODING's encoding named as its"] [258 1 "// codec names itself (UTF-8 is utf-8, latin1 iso8859-1), once the codecs can be looked up (the first standard"] [259 1 "// stream's creation); the name as given when the lookup fails, as before."] [295 1 "// writeStr is TextIOWrapper.write's encoding: utf-8 with strict errors as before, else the codec of PYTHONIOENCODING"] [296 1 "// and the stream's errors handler (a UnicodeEncodeError for an error left strict)."] [300 19 "// reconfigure()'s (queue 286)"] [318 1 "// The site module's exit and quit (site.py's Quitter; _sitebuiltins): calling one raises SystemExit(code)."] [348 1 "// startOrigArgv is sys.orig_argv: bin/pyi python passes the executable and its command line in PYI_ORIG_ARGV (joined"] [349 1 "// by the unit separator), read once and removed from the environment."] [363 1 "// fsDecodeString is a command line's 